comments.text:
Speaking of FreeCell, a couple weeks ago I was visiting my 95yr-old grandmother and noticed she still plays oldschool FreeCell, specifically a variant that's really hard to track down now called FreeCell Pro [
https://cards.fandom.com/wiki/FreeCell_Pro
]
It inspired a weekend project. I always liked that you could swap the card backs in OG FreeCell and play with different "themed" decks, so I vibecoded something a little more modern. I got carried away and added a roguelite mode too (yeah I know how "Roguelite FreeCell" sounds). Anyway, it's free to play on the web, no ads: [
https://freecellworlds.com/
]

I would recommend Cuis Smalltalk (
https://cuis.st
) as a more idiomatic solution that also looks much better due to it's vector graphic based rendering engine.
